  deep snow and the northern lights  the finns love nature so much that they  also socialize outdoors  their traditional dance pavilions are  usually situated by the shores of a lake  or river surrounded by trees  many host ballroom dancing once or twice  a month you can try your foot or  everything from tango to waltz to  traditional finnish dances  and local customs are important here too  the men ask the women to dance  two songs together and then the man  leads the woman back to the side  you don't have to talk when you're  dancing if you don't want to  hurry  up  it depends on whether you come alone or  with  so from the sound of it the locals in  finland know that silence is golden  and that includes out on the dance floor  that's all we have time for today you  can visit us on our facebook page and  let us know your thoughts that's it for  me and and the rest of your remarks crew  for now thanks for watching and we'll  see you tomorrow bye  so  you

